{"availability":"available","full":"GoPlasmatic/datalogic-rs","name":"datalogic-rs","description":"A fast JSONLogic rules engine: one Rust core with official bindings for Node.js, Python, Go, Java, .NET, PHP, and the browser (WASM), plus a React visual debugger.","category":"Business","language":"Rust","stars":91,"forks":13,"created":"2024-11-18T11:08:46Z","updated":"2026-10-01T04:44:52Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://goplasmatic.github.io/datalogic-rs/playground/","topics":["business-rules","declarative-language","dotnet","expression-evaluator","feature-flags","flagd","golang","java","json","jsonlogic","nodejs","openfeature","php","policy-engine","python","rules-engine","rust","templating-engine","wasm","webassembly"],"demo":"https://goplasmatic.github.io/datalogic-rs/playground/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:39.912Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:39.912Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:39.912Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:19:39.912Z","stars":91,"forks":13}],"technologies":["Node.js","Python","Rust","Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Business rules as data. One engine, every runtime.","Write a JSONLogic rule once and evaluate it with the exact same engine in Rust, Node.js, the browser (WASM), Python, Go, Java, .NET, and PHP. One Rust core sits under every binding, so the eight runtimes cannot drift apart, and a rule evaluates in nanoseconds. Store rules as JSON and change pricing, eligibility, and flag logic in production without a redeploy.","[]( []( [](./crates/datalogic-rs/tests/suites/) []("],"features":["🌐 One rule, every runtime: every binding runs the same compiled Rust core, so a rule evaluates with identical semantics on your backend, your edge workers, and your frontend. No cross-language drift, verified by a…","🔒 100% sandbox-safe: evaluate user-submitted rules and formulas without arbitrary code execution. No eval(), no scripting runtime, no I/O; the core forbids unsafe code.","⚡ Nanosecond evaluation: rules compile to OpCode-dispatched programs that run in a reusable memory arena: 10.3 ns geomean, 7.0× the fastest JS engine, 83.6× the reference implementation.","🛠️ Ready-made rule builder: ship a visual editor and step-through debugger to your product dashboard with the companion React component, instead of building rule UI from scratch."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GoPlasmatic/datalogic-rs/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"eb786538bb19706a299e08cdcff78aeec67c892df02daf428aa9db6dec1ea968","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:27:05.760Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:46.260Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-01T04:44:52Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:46.264Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Business rules as data. One engine, every runtime.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GoPlasmatic/datalogic-rs/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"eb786538bb19706a299e08cdcff78aeec67c892df02daf428aa9db6dec1ea968","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GoPlasmatic/datalogic-rs/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:46.260Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GoPlasmatic/datalogic-rs/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:46.261Z","hash":"eb786538bb19706a299e08cdcff78aeec67c892df02daf428aa9db6dec1ea968","originalBytes":15245,"storedBytes":15245,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["rule","rules","data","goplasmatic","engine","every","rust","same","one","readme","readme.md","var","datalogic-rs","binding","bindings","evaluation","npm","datalogic","json","wasm","core","logic","many","native","package","runtime","across","build","evaluate","operators","python","run","add","age","api","apply","arena","benchmark","browser","compile","compiled","conformance","datalogic-node","datalogic-ui","datalogic-wasm","each","edge","eval","feature","jsonlogic","language","license","live","node","node.js","php","plasmatic